## Document Standards

- All documents are Markdown with YAML frontmatter.
- `status: adopted` may appear on a board branch when the file is already in the exact wording that becomes authoritative on merge.
- Use `effective_date: on-merge` when the merge event itself makes the text operative.
- Fillable blanks belong only in `templates/`. Synthetic or incomplete scaffolds are not committed to this repository as if they were adopted records.
- If a record needs a separately certified date, store it in metadata or an accompanying minutes or voting artifact without treating it as the primary adoption authority.

## Relationship to a Working/Drafting Repository (if you maintain one)

Some organizations maintain a separate working or drafting repository —
for agenda preparation, AI agent scratch space, and pre-vote
deliberation — distinct from this repository, which holds only adopted
governance records. If your organization does this, document the
relationship and the promotion path into this repository here. Nothing is
adopted by existing in a drafting space; adoption requires the merge to
`main` in *this* repository.

